IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sss-act`

-- Silver Support Scheme Act 2015 -- worked cases.
--
-- Claims about the ENCODING on stated facts. The s 6(2) deeming rules are the
-- whole of the interesting content, so most of what follows is boundary cases
-- on them.

§ `Fixtures`

`a known birth, 15 June 1960` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS JUST 6
    `day of birth` IS JUST 15

-- s 6(2)(b): born on 29 February.
`born 29 February 1960` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS JUST 2
    `day of birth` IS JUST 29

-- The day after, for comparison.
`born 1 March 1960` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS JUST 3
    `day of birth` IS JUST 1

-- s 6(2)(c): the day cannot be ascertained.
`born in June 1960, day unknown` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS JUST 6
    `day of birth` IS NOTHING

-- s 6(2)(d): the month cannot be ascertained.
`born in 1960, month unknown, day 15` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS NOTHING
    `day of birth` IS JUST 15

-- Both unknown.
`born in 1960, nothing else known` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS NOTHING
    `day of birth` IS NOTHING

`28 February 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 2, `day` IS 28
`1 March 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 3, `day` IS 1
`2 March 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 3, `day` IS 2
`1 January 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 1, `day` IS 1
`15 June 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 6, `day` IS 15
`14 June 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 6, `day` IS 14
`31 December 2024` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2024, `month` IS 12, `day` IS 31

GIVEN `the birth` IS A BirthRecord
GIVETH AN Individual
DECIDE `a qualifying citizen born` `the birth` IS
    Individual WITH
        `name` IS "A"
        `a citizen of Singapore` IS TRUE
        `birth` IS `the birth`
        `satisfies all other prescribed eligibility criteria` IS TRUE

§§ `6(2)(a) -- attainment is ON the anniversary`

-- The anniversary day itself counts: "attains 65 years of age ON the
-- 65th anniversary".
#ASSERT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `14 June 2025`

§§ `6(2)(b) -- the 29 February rule`

-- Born 29 February 1960. The 65th anniversary is deemed to occur on 1 March.
#ASSERT `the deemed date of birth is 29 February` `born 29 February 1960`
#ASSERT `the month of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1960` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the day of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1960` EQUALS 1

#ASSERT NOT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born 29 February 1960`) `28 February 2025`
#ASSERT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born 29 February 1960`) `1 March 2025`

-- THE CONSEQUENCE. A person born on 29 February 1960 and a person born the
-- following day, 1 March 1960, attain 65 on the SAME day. The leap-day person
-- is a day older and becomes eligible no earlier.
#ASSERT `the 65th anniversary as an ordered number` `born 29 February 1960` EQUALS `the 65th anniversary as an ordered number` `born 1 March 1960`

-- And this is not an edge case that sometimes bites: 65 years after a leap year
-- is never itself a leap year, because 65 leaves a remainder of 1 on division
-- by 4. So 29 February never exists on a 65th anniversary, and s 6(2)(b) is not
-- a fallback for an awkward year -- it is the only rule that can ever apply to a
-- 29 February birth. Three leap years, three non-leap anniversaries:
`born 29 February 1956` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1956
    `month of birth` IS JUST 2
    `day of birth` IS JUST 29

`born 29 February 1964` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1964
    `month of birth` IS JUST 2
    `day of birth` IS JUST 29

#ASSERT `the year of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1956` EQUALS 2021
#ASSERT `the year of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1960` EQUALS 2025
#ASSERT `the year of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1964` EQUALS 2029
#ASSERT `the month of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1956` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the month of the 65th anniversary` `born 29 February 1964` EQUALS 3

§§ `6(2)(c) -- the day cannot be ascertained`

-- Deemed born on the first day of the month, so eligibility starts on the 1st.
#ASSERT `the deemed day of birth` `born in June 1960, day unknown` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the deemed month of birth` `born in June 1960, day unknown` EQUALS 6

`1 June 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 6, `day` IS 1
`31 May 2025` MEANS AssessmentDay WITH `year` IS 2025, `month` IS 5, `day` IS 31

#ASSERT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born in June 1960, day unknown`) `1 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born in June 1960, day unknown`) `31 May 2025`

-- The deeming is in the claimant's favour: the same person with a known
-- birthday of 15 June would wait a further fortnight.
#ASSERT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born in June 1960, day unknown`) `14 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `14 June 2025`

§§ `6(2)(d) -- the month cannot be ascertained`

-- Deemed born in January, keeping the known day.
#ASSERT `the deemed month of birth` `born in 1960, month unknown, day 15` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the deemed day of birth` `born in 1960, month unknown, day 15` EQUALS 15

-- Both unknown: 1 January, the earliest the deeming can produce.
#ASSERT `the deemed month of birth` `born in 1960, nothing else known` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the deemed day of birth` `born in 1960, nothing else known` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born in 1960, nothing else known`) `1 January 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has attained 65 years of age` (`a qualifying citizen born` `born in 1960, nothing else known`) `31 December 2024`

-- Where the month is unknown and the day is 29, (d) fires before (b) can:
-- the deemed date is 29 JANUARY, not 29 February, so the leap-day rule never
-- engages. The order the deeming rules apply in decides this, and the Act does
-- not state an order.
`born in 1960, month unknown, day 29` MEANS BirthRecord WITH
    `year of birth` IS 1960
    `month of birth` IS NOTHING
    `day of birth` IS JUST 29

#ASSERT NOT `the deemed date of birth is 29 February` `born in 1960, month unknown, day 29`
#ASSERT `the month of the 65th anniversary` `born in 1960, month unknown, day 29` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the day of the 65th anniversary` `born in 1960, month unknown, day 29` EQUALS 29

§§ `6(1) -- the three limbs together`

`a non-citizen born 15 June 1960` MEANS Individual WITH
    `name` IS "B"
    `a citizen of Singapore` IS FALSE
    `birth` IS `a known birth, 15 June 1960`
    `satisfies all other prescribed eligibility criteria` IS TRUE

`a citizen failing the prescribed criteria` MEANS Individual WITH
    `name` IS "C"
    `a citizen of Singapore` IS TRUE
    `birth` IS `a known birth, 15 June 1960`
    `satisfies all other prescribed eligibility criteria` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the individual is an eligible individual` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual is an eligible individual` `a non-citizen born 15 June 1960` `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual is an eligible individual` `a citizen failing the prescribed criteria` `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT NOT `the individual is an eligible individual` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `14 June 2025`

-- s 7 adds nothing to eligibility: it turns on being an eligible individual and
-- leaves the amount to regulations.
#ASSERT `the individual is eligible to receive benefits under section 7` (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`) `15 June 2025`

§§ `10 -- recovery`

`an overpayment to an eligible recipient` MEANS Disbursement WITH
    `the recipient` IS (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`)
    `disbursed as a cash grant` IS TRUE
    `the amount paid` IS 900
    `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive` IS 600
    `eligible for this particular cash grant` IS TRUE
    `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE

`a grant to someone not eligible at all` MEANS Disbursement WITH
    `the recipient` IS `a non-citizen born 15 June 1960`
    `disbursed as a cash grant` IS TRUE
    `the amount paid` IS 600
    `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive` IS 600
    `eligible for this particular cash grant` IS TRUE
    `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE

`a correct payment` MEANS Disbursement WITH
    `the recipient` IS (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`)
    `disbursed as a cash grant` IS TRUE
    `the amount paid` IS 600
    `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive` IS 600
    `eligible for this particular cash grant` IS TRUE
    `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE

-- Only the excess goes back where the recipient was entitled to something.
#ASSERT `an amount is recoverable under section 10(1)` `an overpayment to an eligible recipient` `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable under section 10(1)` `an overpayment to an eligible recipient` `15 June 2025` EQUALS 300

-- The whole payment goes back where the recipient was not an eligible
-- individual, even though the amount itself was the right one.
#ASSERT `an amount is recoverable under section 10(1)` `a grant to someone not eligible at all` `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT `the amount recoverable under section 10(1)` `a grant to someone not eligible at all` `15 June 2025` EQUALS 600

#ASSERT NOT `an amount is recoverable under section 10(1)` `a correct payment` `15 June 2025`

-- s 10(2) does not read s 6 at all: "whether or not an eligible individual".
`a correct payment obtained by a lie` MEANS Disbursement WITH
    `the recipient` IS (`a qualifying citizen born` `a known birth, 15 June 1960`)
    `disbursed as a cash grant` IS TRUE
    `the amount paid` IS 600
    `the amount the recipient is eligible to receive` IS 600
    `eligible for this particular cash grant` IS TRUE
    `obtained by knowingly or recklessly making a false or misleading statement` IS TRUE
    `obtained by producing a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `an amount is recoverable under section 10(1)` `a correct payment obtained by a lie` `15 June 2025`
#ASSERT `an amount is recoverable under section 10(2)` `a correct payment obtained by a lie`

§§ `11 -- the offence needs both limbs`

`a lie with dishonest intent that obtained a grant` MEANS AllegedOffence WITH
    `knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` IS TRUE
    `produced or provided a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE
    `acted with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS TRUE

-- A lie that obtained nothing: limb (b) fails, so no offence under s 11 --
-- though s 10(2) may still recover anything that was in fact obtained.
`a lie that obtained nothing` MEANS AllegedOffence WITH
    `knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` IS TRUE
    `produced or provided a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE
    `acted with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine` IS TRUE
    `dishonestly obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS FALSE

-- An innocent mistake that did obtain a grant: limb (a) and the intent fail.
`an honest mistake that obtained a grant` MEANS AllegedOffence WITH
    `knowingly or recklessly made a false or misleading statement` IS FALSE
    `produced or provided a document known or which ought reasonably to be known to be false in a material particular` IS FALSE
    `acted with the intention of dishonestly inducing another person to accept it as genuine` IS FALSE
    `dishonestly obtained a cash grant or other benefit under the Scheme` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 11` `a lie with dishonest intent that obtained a grant`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 11` `a lie that obtained nothing`
#ASSERT `paragraph (a) of section 11(1) is made out` `a lie that obtained nothing`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is guilty of an offence under section 11` `an honest mistake that obtained a grant`

§§ `12 -- the power on conviction`

#ASSERT `the court may make a section 12 order` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a section 12 order` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the court may make a section 12 order` FALSE TRUE
